it('deletes the project', async () => {
  const res = await request(app).delete('/projects/42').expect(204);
  expect(res.text).toBe('');
});
```
## 8. Conclusion

HTTP 204 means the request worked and there is nothing to send back. Use it for deletes and updates when the client needs no data. Send no body and no *Content-Length*, but feel free to send headers such as a new *ETag*. A client checks for HTTP 204 before reading the body, and keeps its current view. The full list of HTTP status codes links to the other articles.
